  "provenance": {
    "pattern": "trip-hop at half time: the kick on one with a pickup on two-and, the snare on three alone, open-ish hats on the ands, a held sub, and a long dark chord every two bars",
    "knowledge": "public knowledge of the genre: the pattern as drummers, producers and tutorials commonly write it; no recording was sampled, transcribed from audio or mined",
    "note": "Two bars: kick one, two-and; one, two-and, four-a as a pickup into the next one; the snare on three only, so a bar of four is felt as two slow beats; the loose hat on every and, swung and late. The bass is held on the root under the harmony; a dark struck keyboard chord sounds on one every two bars and rings most of the way. Played under the Trip Hop tile's spell at 85-95 (round G4).",
